    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The power dispatching agency is responsible for scheduling generation based on market contract execution rates, conducting safety checks, managing grid operations, and adjusting plans due to grid security or renewable energy integration needs.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The power trading agency is responsible for organizing transactions, providing settlement basis, publishing transmission capacity data, and handling contract transfers and adjustments; it also coordinates with the dispatching agency for safety validation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"发电企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Generation enterprises are market participants that must adhere to contract execution targets, face deviation penalties, and may engage in post-contract electricity transfer transactions if their contracts are unbalanced.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Electricity users are market participants whose actual consumption exceeding planned levels results in overuse charges; they participate in contract adjustments and are subject to deviation assessments.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"宁夏发展改革委员会\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Ningxia Development and Reform Commission is a regulatory body to which the dispatching agency must report during emergency situations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"西北能源监管局\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Northwest Energy Regulatory Bureau is another regulatory authority that receives written reports from the dispatching agency after emergencies.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电网企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Grid companies are responsible for installing metering devices, collecting and submitting metering data, settling electricity bills, and managing proxy purchase electricity costs and related fees.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"储能\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Energy storage owned by electricity users can lead to deviation in contract execution, which the user must bear personally.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"需求侧响应\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Demand-side response programs allow electricity users to adjust consumption during specific periods, resulting in deviations that are self-managed by the user.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"优先发电计划\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Priority generation plans are government-mandated allocations of electricity production that must be scheduled without being concentrated in specific time slots or used as tools for market manipulation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"市场以外的电量\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Electricity outside the market refers to non-market-based power usage that is included in deviation calculations for both generators and users.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"偏差考核\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Deviation assessment refers to financial penalties imposed on market participants when actual output or consumption differs from contracted amounts, based on regional supply-demand balance.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"合同转让交易\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Contract transfer transactions occur monthly (15–20th) and allow parties to reallocate contract volumes, with prices not exceeding original transaction values and no impact on power plant settlement prices.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"月度安全校核\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Monthly safety validation is a process conducted by the dispatching agency to ensure grid stability; if failed, transactions are reduced according to predefined rules.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"实时调度\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Real-time dispatching involves daily tracking of total contract execution rates across generating units to maintain parity among similar types.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"中长期交易计划调整\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Adjustments to medium- and long-term transaction plans may be made by the dispatching agency due to grid safety or clean energy integration requirements.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"紧急情况调度\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"In cases of system emergencies, the dispatching agency may prioritize safety and implement immediate dispatching actions, later reporting to regulatory authorities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"结算依据\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Settlement basis is provided by the trading agency and includes details such as actual settlement volume, contract electricity and pricing, deviation charges, and balance account information.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"代理购电价格\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Proxy purchase price is calculated monthly and published three days in advance, applied to actual consumption and settled fully each month.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"平衡账户\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The balance account manages settlement differences including optimization outages, excess generation, overuse charges, and deviation penalty fees, with annual clearance.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"预挂牌月平衡偏差方式\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A settlement method where monthly imbalance is managed through pre-opening bidding, following national medium- and long-term trading rules.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"上下调预挂牌价格\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Pre-bidding prices for upward and downward adjustments are used to settle deviation power generated by proxy purchasing activities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"场内集中竞价出清价格\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The most recent, shortest-cycle clearing price from an internal centralized bidding process is used for settlement when pre-bidding is unavailable.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"非不可抗力因素\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Non-force majeure causes such as grid faults or upgrades result in deviation responsibility falling on the grid company.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"不可抗力因素\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Force majeure events, such as natural disasters, exempt participants from deviation penalties.\")##\n\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"The dispatching agency provides operational data and constraints to the trading agency, which uses this information to conduct transaction clearing and safety validation.\" <|>\"coordination, grid operation\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"发电企业\"<|>\"The dispatching agency schedules generation plans based on contract execution rates and adjusts them due to grid safety or renewable integration needs, affecting generator performance.\" <|>\"scheduling, operational control\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"The dispatching agency indirectly influences user behavior by managing grid load and ensuring balance, especially through real-time monitoring and emergency measures.\" <|>\"grid management, demand influence\"<|>6)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"宁夏发展改革委员会\"<|>\"The dispatching agency must submit written reports to the Ningxia Development and Reform Commission after implementing emergency dispatch actions.\" <|>\"regulatory reporting, emergency compliance\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"西北能源监管局\"<|>\"The dispatching agency must provide written explanations to the Northwest Energy Regulatory Bureau regarding unsatisfied safety checks.\" <|>\"regulatory transparency, oversight\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"发电企业\"<|>\"The trading agency manages contract execution, facilitates contract transfers, and provides settlement data; generators must comply with deviation rules and participate in adjustments.\" <|>\"contract management, settlement processing\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"The trading agency determines settlement terms for users, including deviation charges and overuse pricing, and enables contract adjustments under agreed conditions.\" <|>\"billing, contractual obligations\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"电网企业\"<|>\"The trading agency relies on grid companies to provide accurate metering data and supports billing processes involving grid-level settlements.\" <|>\"data sharing, settlement support\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电网企业\"<|>\"发电企业\"<|>\"Grid companies collect metering data from generators and settle electricity payments, forming part of the broader financial and technical infrastructure.\" <|>\"metering, payment settlement\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电网企业\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"Grid companies bill users based on actual consumption, applying tariffs such as basic rates, time-of-use pricing, and power factor adjustments.\" <|>\"billing