    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"宁夏回族自治区电力中长期交易规则\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A regulatory document outlining the framework for medium- and long-term power market transactions in Ningxia Hui Autonomous Region, designed to establish a unified, open, competitive, and orderly electricity market based on national policies and local conditions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"中共中央国务院关于进一步深化电力体制改革的若干意见\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A national policy document (Central Document No. 9, 2015) that provides foundational guidance for electricity market reform in China, cited as a basis for the development of the Ningxia rule.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国家发展改革委国家能源局关于印发<电力中长期交易基本规则>的通知\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A regulatory notification issued by the National Development and Reform Commission and the National Energy Administration (Document No. 889, 2020), which serves as a reference for the formulation of regional electricity trading rules.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国家能源局西北监管局\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The Northwest Regulatory Branch of the State Energy Administration, responsible for supervising the power market and transaction institutions in Ningxia, with authority to perform regulatory duties according to its functional responsibilities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"宁夏回族自治区发展和改革委员会\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The Development and Reform Commission of Ningxia Hui Autonomous Region, one of the two primary regulatory bodies overseeing medium- and long-term power market operations and transactions within the region.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"发电企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Entities engaged in power generation that are eligible to participate in the electricity market, subject to legal and technical requirements such as obtaining permits, meeting environmental standards, and complying with grid connection regulations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"售电企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Companies authorized to sell electricity to end-users, including distribution and retail power providers, required to register with the power trading institution and comply with disclosure and credit obligations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"End-users of electricity, including industrial and commercial consumers, who may directly participate in the market or be served through grid companies if unable to join directly; must meet technical and financial criteria.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"储能企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Entities involved in energy storage systems that are recognized as valid participants in the power market under the rule, capable of contributing to grid stability and flexibility.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电网企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Electricity transmission and distribution companies responsible for maintaining grid safety, providing fair access and services, collecting fees, and ensuring supply continuity for non-market users.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"An institutional body responsible for organizing market transactions, managing platforms and contracts, registering market participants, providing settlement data, monitoring market behavior, and supporting regulatory functions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"An entity responsible for real-time grid operation, system balance, security checks, and providing critical operational data to support market execution and coordination with the power trading institution.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力辅助服务市场（补偿）机制\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A separate mechanism related to ancillary services in the power system, currently not covered by this rule but planned for future development.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"双边协商\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A method of conducting power transactions where two parties negotiate directly to reach an agreement on price and volume.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"集中交易\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A form of power transaction involving organized market mechanisms such as listing, centralized bidding, and rolling matching, conducted through a central platform.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"挂牌\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A type of centralized trading method where participants publicly list their buy or sell offers, allowing others to accept or counter them.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"集中竞价\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A trading mechanism where multiple participants submit bids and offers simultaneously, and prices are determined through competitive auction principles.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"滚动撮合\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A dynamic matching process in electricity trading where buy and sell orders are continuously matched over time until no further matches can be made.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"多年、年、季、月、周、多日等执行日前（不含）以上的多日电力（电量）批发交易\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"A category of power transactions defined by duration (ranging from years down to multi-day periods) and executed prior to the day-ahead market, intended for wholesale electricity delivery.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"优先发电计划\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A policy-driven mechanism ensuring certain power generation sources (e.g., renewable energy, base-load plants) are dispatched first, regardless of market price, to fulfill national energy and environmental goals.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"公平的输电服务和电网接入服务\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A principle requiring all market participants to receive equitable access to transmission networks and grid connection facilities without discrimination.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力调度机构的统一调度\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The requirement that all grid-connected entities must follow instructions from the power dispatching authority to maintain system stability and reliability.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"清洁能源消纳责任\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A regulatory obligation imposed on market participants to consume clean energy (such as wind and solar) in accordance with national policies and avoid curtailment.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"市场管理委员会\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"A governing body established to discuss major issues in the power market, organize meetings periodically, and contribute to decision-making and rule evaluation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"市场主体注册管理\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The process by which market participants must register with the power trading institution to gain eligibility to engage in transactions, with specific procedures depending on the type of participant.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"交易结算依据\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Information and documentation provided by the power trading institution to support billing and settlement, including total electricity costs, auxiliary service fees, and transmission charges.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"数据交互与网络安全\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Regulatory requirements mandating secure data exchange between the power trading institution and the dispatching agency, in compliance with national cybersecurity standards.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"宁夏回族自治区电力中长期交易规则\"<|>\"中共中央国务院关于进一步深化电力体制改革的若干意见\"<|>\"The Ningxia rule is developed based on the national policy framework established by the Central Document No. 9, 2015, which mandates market-oriented reforms in the power sector.\"<|>\"regulatory foundation, policy alignment\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"宁夏回族自治区电力中长期交易规则\"<|>\"国家发展改革委国家能源局关于印发<电力中长期交易基本规则>的通知\"<|>\"The Ningxia rule references the national basic rule issued by NDRC and NEA (Document No. 889, 2020), indicating it follows a standardized model for medium- and long-term trading.\"<|>\"regulatory alignment, procedural standardization\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家能源局西北监管局\"<|>\"宁夏回族自治区发展和改革委员会\"<|>\"Both entities jointly exercise regulatory oversight over the Ningxia power market and trading institutions, sharing responsibility for enforcing market rules.\"<|>\"joint regulation, shared governance\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"发电企业\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"These two types of entities are core participants in direct power transactions, engaging in buying and selling electricity through various market mechanisms like bilateral negotiation and centralized trading.\"<|>\"market participation, transactional relationship\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"售电企业\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"Selling companies act as intermediaries between generators and end-users, signing contracts and managing demand-side information, especially for those not directly participating in the market.\"<|>\"intermediary role, contract management\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电网企业\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"Grid operators must comply with dispatch instructions and collaborate closely with the dispatching authority to ensure real-time balance and system safety.\"<|>\"operational coordination, grid management\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"The trading institution relies on the dispatching agency for critical data such as security constraints, available transmission capacity, and unit commitments to enable accurate market clearing and execution.\"<|>\"data dependency, operational synergy\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"市场管理委员会\"<|>\"The trading institution organizes and facilitates meetings of the Market Management Committee to discuss significant policy and operational matters, enabling collective governance.\"<|>\"governance collaboration, institutional coordination\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"市场主体\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"All market participants must register with the power trading institution to gain access to the market, and the institution manages their enrollment, data provision, and compliance monitoring.\"<|>\"access control, registration management\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"清洁能源消纳责任\"<|>\"Electricity users are legally obligated to support the consumption of clean energy, aligning with national green energy targets and requiring active participation in sustainable usage.\"<|>\"compliance obligation, environmental responsibility\"<|>6)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"售电企业\"<|>\"信息披露义务\"<|>\"Selling companies are required to disclose financial status, assets, credit commitments, and major events via official websites, promoting transparency and trust in the market.\"<|>\"transparency, regulatory compliance\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"发电企业\"<|>\"优先发电计划\"<|>\"Power generators must adhere to the priority dispatch schedule, espec