mation security level three protection standards.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国家能源局及其派出机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The National Energy Administration and its dispatched institutions are responsible for receiving periodic market monitoring reports from the trading and dispatching institutions and overseeing market integrity.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"自治区及以上人民政府\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The autonomous region-level or higher governments have the authority to declare emergency states during major disasters or supply-demand imbalances, suspend market trading, and exempt market participants from contractual liabilities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"仲裁委员会\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Arbitration committees serve as an alternative dispute resolution mechanism for electricity market conflicts when negotiations fail.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"人民法院\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The People's Courts are legal bodies where market participants can file lawsuits to resolve disputes arising from electricity market transactions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"社会公众信息\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Social public information refers to data disclosed to the general public, including laws, regulations, policy documents, electricity trading processes, and basic market operation data.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"市场公开信息\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Market public information includes details accessible to all market participants, such as entity registration status, generation equipment data, grid operating conditions, transaction forecasts, execution reports, and settlement summaries.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"私有信息\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Private information is restricted to specific market entities and includes sensitive data like generator performance parameters, user consumption profiles, bid details, trade outcomes, and contract settlements.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"信息披露\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Information disclosure refers to the systematic release of regulated data across different categories (public, open, private) by authorized institutions to ensure transparency and fairness in the electricity market.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"市场干预\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Market intervention occurs when the trading or dispatching institutions take actions such as issuing guidance, modifying rules, or adjusting trades due to emergencies, systemic failures, or rule violations that threaten market stability.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"重大事故危及电网安全\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"A major incident endangering grid safety triggers immediate market intervention to restore stability and prevent cascading failures.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"应急状态或紧急状态\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"An emergency state declared by the government allows suspension of market operations, directive execution of power generation and usage plans, and exemption from contractual obligations during severe supply-demand imbalances.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"市场监控分析报告\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Regular market monitoring analysis reports are submitted by trading and dispatching institutions to regulatory bodies to assess risks and ensure compliance with market rules.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力交易业务流程\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The process of electricity trading includes registration, bidding, clearing, settlement, and execution phases, governed by established procedures and rules.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"发电侧上网电价\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The on-grid price for power generation is set by the state and forms part of the social public information disclosed to the public.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"输配电价\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Transmission and distribution prices are regulated rates that determine the cost of delivering electricity through the grid and are included in publicly disclosed information.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"政府性基金及附加\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Government funds and surcharges are levied to support energy policies and are part of the information disclosed to the public.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"系统备用费\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"System reserve fees are charges applied to maintain grid reliability and are included in publicly available tariff information.\")##\n(\"relationsh